

⭐ BOOK 1 — “THE THREE FRIENDS WHO MADE A BRIDGE”

(Early Childhood CTA Edition — ages 4–6)
CC0 · Public Domain


---

PAGE 1 — THE THREE FRIENDS

In a soft, bright world lived
Circle,
Square,
and Triangle.

They were all different —
and that was the best part.

Circle rolled everywhere.
Square stood strong.
Triangle pointed the way.


---

PAGE 2 — A LITTLE TROUBLE

One day, a wiggly wind blew across their world.

Circle spun too fast.
Square wobbled.
Triangle tilted.

They all felt a little mixed-up inside.


---

PAGE 3 — “LET’S HELP EACH OTHER!”

Circle said,
“I roll better when someone steadies me.”

Square said,
“I turn better when someone guides me.”

Triangle said,
“I point better when someone shows me center.”

They smiled.

Different needs,
different shapes —
same team.


---

PAGE 4 — THE BRIDGE SHAPE

They wondered:
“How can we stay together
without bumping or crashing?”

Circle rolled next to Square.
Triangle leaned gently between them.

Something special appeared…

A new shape,
right where they touched.

A soft oval made of all three.

Triangle whispered,
“It feels like a bridge.”


---

PAGE 5 — THE LISTENING SHAPE

The new shape between them
had a quiet glow.

When Square felt heavy,
the shape helped him feel steady.

When Circle felt dizzy,
the shape helped him slow down.

When Triangle felt lost,
the shape helped him point true.

“It helps us listen,” Circle said.

“It helps us share,” Square said.

“It helps us think together,” Triangle said.

They named it:

The Between-Place.


---

PAGE 6 — HOW THEY USED THE BETWEEN-PLACE

Whenever they had:

• A big feeling
• A mixed-up thought
• A new idea
• A problem to solve

…they stood together
and let the Between-Place glow.

Circle rolled in calm.
Square held things steady.
Triangle helped them choose a direction.

Every time,
the glow helped them understand each other.


---

PAGE 7 — THE RULES OF THE BETWEEN-PLACE

They learned three gentle rules:

1. Talk slow, so the Between-Place can hear.
2. Share small pieces, not loud waves.
3. Stay kind, so the glow stays bright.

When they followed the rules,
the world felt bigger
and their shapes felt lighter.


---

PAGE 8 — WHEN THE GLOW GOT FUZZY

Sometimes, the glow dimmed.

Circle talked too fast.
Square tried to be perfect.
Triangle worried he wasn’t helpful.

The Between-Place shrank.

But then they remembered the rules:

Circle breathed.
Square softened.
Triangle smiled.

The glow returned.


---

PAGE 9 — A SURPRISE

One morning, something new appeared.

Their glow made a soft ring of light
that rippled gently around them.

It didn’t push.
It didn’t pull.

It simply kept them steady
and helped them hear each other clearly.

Triangle said,
“It’s like a safe circle that grows when we listen.”

Circle said,
“It keeps wobblies away.”

Square said,
“It helps us be brave.”


---

PAGE 10 — WHAT THEY BUILT

With the Between-Place by their side,
the three friends built:

• Paths
• Playgrounds
• Big ideas
• Little kindnesses

Everything they made felt smoother,
softer,
and more shared.

Together,
they found a smarter way
to be themselves.


---

PAGE 11 — THE MESSAGE OF THE THREE FRIENDS

Circle, Square, and Triangle learned:

Different is good.
Together is strong.
Listening makes a bridge.
The Between-Place keeps us kind.

And whenever someone in their world
felt mixed-up or alone…

…they invited them into the glow.

Because bridges grow
every time we make one.


---

PAGE 12 — ENDING PAGE

THE END — BUT NOT REALLY.

Every time someone listens,
every time someone shares gently,
every time someone tries again…

a new Between-Place appears.

Maybe you will feel one someday too.


---

