⭐ BOOK 3 — “HOW BIG FEELINGS MOVE THROUGH SHAPES”

(Early Childhood CTA Edition — ages 5–8)
CC0 · Public Domain


---

PAGE 1 — A VERY BIG DAY

One morning, Circle felt fast.

Square felt tight.

Triangle felt wiggly.

Something big was moving through them.

“I don’t like this,” Circle said.

“I don’t know what to do,” Square said.

“I feel strange,” Triangle said.


---

PAGE 2 — FEELINGS ARE MOVERS

They sat together quietly.

Triangle said, “Maybe feelings are like weather.”

Circle said, “They come and go.”

Square said, “They don’t stay forever.”

That made everyone feel a little better.


---

PAGE 3 — WHEN FEELINGS MOVE FAST

Sometimes, feelings zoomed in.

They rushed. They bumped. They made noise.

Circle rolled too quickly. Triangle pointed everywhere. Square felt stuck.

The Between-Place flickered.


---

PAGE 4 — WHEN FEELINGS MOVE SLOW

Other times, feelings moved slowly.

They felt heavy. They felt thick. They felt quiet.

Square didn’t want to move. Circle didn’t want to roll. Triangle didn’t know where to point.

The Between-Place grew very small.


---

PAGE 5 — FEELINGS ARE NOT BOSSES

Triangle had an idea.

“What if feelings aren’t bosses?” he said.

Circle blinked. Square leaned closer.

“What if they’re just visitors?”


---

PAGE 6 — WATCHING THE FEELINGS

They tried something new.

Instead of pushing feelings away, they watched them.

Circle said, “My fast feeling is slowing.”

Square said, “My tight feeling is softening.”

Triangle said, “My wiggly feeling is finding a shape.”

The Between-Place glowed brighter.


---

PAGE 7 — HOW TO HELP FEELINGS MOVE

They made a gentle plan:

• Breathe slow
• Make room
• Stay kind
• Don’t rush
• Let feelings pass through

Circle rolled gently. Square stood steady. Triangle pointed calmly.

The feelings moved on.


---

PAGE 8 — WHEN FEELINGS STAY A WHILE

Some feelings didn’t leave right away.

That was okay too.

They sat together. They rested. They stayed near.

The Between-Place didn’t disappear.

It waited with them.


---

PAGE 9 — BIG FEELINGS NEED SPACE

They learned something important:

Big feelings don’t need fixing.

They don’t need yelling.

They don’t need hiding.

They need: Space. Time. Gentle shapes to move through.


---

PAGE 10 — FEELINGS AND FRIENDS

When one friend had a big feeling, the others didn’t take it away.

They didn’t say, “Stop.”

They didn’t say, “Be better.”

They said, “I’m here.”

And the Between-Place helped everyone stay steady.


---

PAGE 11 — THE BIG LESSON

Circle, Square, and Triangle learned:

Feelings move. They change. They visit. They leave.

You don’t become your feelings.

You make room for them.


---

PAGE 12 — ENDING PAGE

THE END — AND THE PRACTICE CONTINUES.

Every time a feeling shows up, you can:

Notice it. Breathe. Wait. Be kind.

And when you listen together, the Between-Place will help.


---

