⭐ BOOK 4 — “THE FIVE FRIENDS WHO SING TOGETHER”

(Early Childhood CTA Edition — ages 6–9)
CC0 · Public Domain


---

PAGE 1 — FIVE FRIENDS

Circle, Square, and Triangle were playing when three new friends arrived:

Star, who sparkled softly.
Line, who stretched calmly.

Now there were five.

Five shapes. Five voices. Five ways to be.


---

PAGE 2 — TOO MANY VOICES

Everyone wanted to share at once.

Circle rolled fast. Triangle pointed quickly. Square spoke carefully. Star shined brightly. Line stretched long.

It got loud. It got busy.

The Between-Place tried to glow…

…but it flickered.


---

PAGE 3 — A LITTLE QUIET

Square said, “It’s hard to hear.”

Triangle said, “I don’t know where to point.”

Star dimmed a little. Line stopped stretching.

Circle whispered, “Maybe we need space.”


---

PAGE 4 — LISTENING FOR THE SONG

They sat together quietly.

No one pushed. No one pulled.

They listened.

Not just with ears — but with patience.

Something gentle began to happen.


---

PAGE 5 — ONE VOICE AT A TIME

Circle rolled slowly and shared first.

Then Square spoke.

Triangle pointed after.

Star sparkled softly.

Line stretched at the end.

Each voice had its turn.

The Between-Place glowed wider.


---

PAGE 6 — NOT THE SAME, BUT TOGETHER

They noticed something special.

They didn’t all sound the same.

Circle was round and rolling. Square was steady and strong. Triangle was sharp and clear. Star was bright and playful. Line was calm and smooth.

Different sounds. One song.


---

PAGE 7 — WHEN SOMEONE IS QUIET

Sometimes, one friend stayed quiet.

That was okay.

The song didn’t break.

The Between-Place stayed bright.

Triangle said, “Quiet is part of the song too.”


---

PAGE 8 — WHEN SOMEONE IS LOUD

Sometimes, one friend got loud.

That was okay too.

The others listened.

Circle said, “Loud feelings pass.”

Square said, “We can wait.”

The song found its balance again.


---

PAGE 9 — HOW THEY SING TOGETHER

They made a few gentle rules:

• Take turns
• Leave space
• Listen more than speak
• Let quiet be quiet
• Let loud be loud

The rules didn’t stop the song.

They made the song.


---

PAGE 10 — A BIGGER GLOW

The Between-Place grew larger than before.

It wasn’t just between two friends.

It wrapped around all five.

A soft, steady hum filled the air.

Star smiled, “This feels like singing.”


---

PAGE 11 — THE BIG LESSON

The five friends learned:

You don’t need to sound the same to belong.

You don’t need to be first to matter.

When everyone has space, the song finds itself.


---

PAGE 12 — ENDING PAGE

THE END — AND THE CHORUS CONTINUES.

Every group has a song.

When we listen, take turns, and leave space…

we can sing together — even when we’re different.


---

